<BaseLayout title="Privacy | Low Value Content" description="How Low Value Content handles information on the pre-launch Royal House of Engagement website.">
  <article class="plain-page">
    <header><p class="eyebrow">Draft · October 16, 2026</p><h1>Privacy.</h1><p>The current public experience is intentionally simple: no customer accounts, marketing forms, advertising pixels, or behavioral analytics have been added.</p></header>
    <div class="rows">
    <section><h2>Information collected</h2><p>Low Value Content does not currently ask general visitors to submit personal information through this website. The hosting provider may process ordinary technical request information—such as IP address, browser information, requested page, and timestamp—to deliver and secure the site.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Restricted environments</h2><p>Development and staging versions use Google and Firebase authentication. An authorized email address may be retained in session storage for the current browser session. This access gate is not used on the public production site.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Third parties</h2><p>The public pages use locally hosted images, styles, and scripts. Future links to social profiles and any restricted test checkout lead to independent services whose own privacy terms apply.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Future features</h2><p>Before email capture, analytics, customer accounts, public payments, or commerce are introduced, this notice will be updated to identify the information involved, its purpose, providers, retention, choices, and relevant rights.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Contact</h2><p>A dedicated privacy contact has not yet been published. The Support page will be updated with an approved, monitored destination before the site begins collecting customer information.</p></section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
